From 6da5cdb26b844d6032a19ed9010dfd7e180326ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mesa-nvk-horizon <mesa-nvk-horizon@localhost>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 22:37:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] util/detect_os: add DETECT_OS_HORIZON
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Horizon OS (Nintendo Switch), reached through devkitA64 and libnx,
matched no branch in detect_os.h, so every DETECT_OS_* was 0. Code that
picks between a POSIX and a Windows path then reaches neither and hits
its #error, or silently compiles the wrong branch.

__SWITCH__ is the marker devkitPro's toolchain defines for it, and is
what the whole Switch homebrew ecosystem identifies the platform by.

POSIX_LITE rather than POSIX, which is the distinction the macro exists
for and matches what newlib actually provides here: <unistd.h>,
<time.h>, <sys/time.h>, <sched.h> and <errno.h> are present, while
<syslog.h>, <sys/shm.h> and any dynamic loader are not. Fuchsia is
declared the same way.

Nothing else changes: this only fills in a case that previously fell
through, so no existing platform's macros move.

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 3 item 1 (OS detection) — a DEVIATION from this
  session's item 3 scope, kept to the minimum item 5 needed and
  recorded in STATUS.md. Nothing else from item 1 is included.
Why: util/os_time.c dispatches on DETECT_OS_*, and with every macro 0
  it cannot select any implementation.
Evidence: building src/util for aarch64/horizon fails with
    os_time.c:52:4: error: #error Unsupported OS
    os_time.c:99:4: error: #error Unsupported OS
  Measured for the POSIX_LITE choice: <syslog.h> is absent from
  devkitA64's newlib, <sys/time.h> and <sched.h> are present, and
  configure reports Check usable header "sys/shm.h" : NO and
  "dlfcn.h" : NO.
Upstream: yes, once a Horizon port exists to justify it — it is
  additive and cannot change any current platform's detection.
---
 src/util/detect_os.h | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/util/detect_os.h b/src/util/detect_os.h
index 7403724..b59b6ce 100644
--- a/src/util/detect_os.h
+++ b/src/util/detect_os.h
@@ -91,6 +91,19 @@
 #define DETECT_OS_POSIX 1
 #endif
 
+/*
+ * Horizon OS (Nintendo Switch), through devkitA64/libnx. __SWITCH__ is
+ * the marker devkitPro's toolchain adds for it.
+ *
+ * POSIX_LITE, not POSIX: newlib provides <unistd.h>, <time.h>,
+ * <sys/time.h>, <sched.h> and <errno.h>, but there is no <syslog.h>,
+ * no <sys/shm.h> and no dynamic loader.
+ */
+#if defined(__SWITCH__)
+#define DETECT_OS_HORIZON 1
+#define DETECT_OS_POSIX_LITE 1
+#endif
+
 
 /*
  * Make sure DETECT_OS_* are always defined, so that they can be used with #if
@@ -119,6 +132,9 @@
 #ifndef DETECT_OS_FUCHSIA
 #define DETECT_OS_FUCHSIA 0
 #endif
+#ifndef DETECT_OS_HORIZON
+#define DETECT_OS_HORIZON 0
+#endif
 #ifndef DETECT_OS_HURD
 #define DETECT_OS_HURD 0
 #endif
